---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { BREW_INSTALL, LATEST_VERSION, NODE_VERSION, PLATFORMS, docs, downloadUrl, repo } from "../site";

const released = LATEST_VERSION !== null;
const groups = (["macOS", "Linux", "Windows"] as const).map((os) => ({
  os,
  platforms: PLATFORMS.filter((p) => p.os === os),
}));
---

<Base
  title="Download"
  description="Download Magnetite for macOS and Linux: signed releases. Windows is in preparation."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Download" title='Get <span class="text-brass">Magnetite</span>' />
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 pt-12">

    {
      released ? (
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          The latest release is version {LATEST_VERSION}. Magnetite is developed and used daily on macOS with Apple
          silicon; the packages for Intel Macs and Linux are experimental. Expect breaking changes, including to the data
          on disk. All files, checksums and release notes are on <a href={repo.releases} class="link">GitHub Releases</a>.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <div class="glass flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border-accent/40! p-6">
          <Icon name="bell" size={20} class="mt-0.5 text-accent" />
          <div class="leading-relaxed text-secondary">
            <p class="font-semibold text-fg">Coming soon: no release yet.</p>
            <p class="mt-1">
              Today Magnetite runs on macOS with Apple silicon, built from source. Signed downloads will appear on this
              page and on <a href={repo.releases} class="link">GitHub Releases</a>, macOS first, then Linux and Windows.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      )
    }

    <section aria-labelledby="platforms-title" class="mt-14">
      <h2 id="platforms-title" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">Platforms</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-8">
        {
          groups.map((g) => (
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">{g.os}</h3>
              <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
                {g.platforms.map((p) => {
                  const url = downloadUrl(p);
                  return (
                    <li class="card spot flex flex-col gap-4 p-6" data-reveal>
                      <div>
                        <p class="text-lg font-semibold">
                          {p.os} <span class="font-normal text-secondary">· {p.arch}</span>
                        </p>
                        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-secondary">{p.status}</p>
                        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">{p.requirements}</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
                        {url ? (
                          <a href={url} class="btn btn-primary">
                            <Icon name="download" size={17} />
                            Download
                          </a>
                        ) : (
                          <span class="btn btn-soon">Coming soon</span>
                        )}
                        <code class="font-mono text-xs break-all text-muted">
                          {p.asset(url && LATEST_VERSION ? LATEST_VERSION : "<version>")}
                        </code>
                      </div>
                    </li>
                  );
                })}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="brew-title" class="mt-16">
      <h2 id="brew-title" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">Homebrew</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        On macOS, Magnetite will be available from its own Homebrew tap{released ? " soon" : " once the first release is out"}:
      </p>
      <code class="code-block mt-4">{BREW_INSTALL}</code>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="linux-title" class="mt-16">
      <h2 id="linux-title" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">Linux notes</h2>
      <div class="prose mt-3">
        <p>
          The Linux build is a folder you unpack and start with <code>./magnetite</code>. It needs the libraries any Chromium
          browser needs (GTK 3, NSS, ALSA, GBM, libdrm, xkbcommon), and Chromium’s sandbox needs user namespaces. On Ubuntu
          23.10 and later that takes an AppArmor profile. The package’s <a href={docs.linux}>README</a> has the commands.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="source-title" class="mt-16">
      <h2 id="source-title" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">Build from source</h2>
      <div class="prose mt-3">
        <p>
          On a Mac with Apple silicon you can build Magnetite today. You need Rust, the Xcode command line tools, Node
          {NODE_VERSION} or later, CMake and Ninja; a one-time step downloads the Chromium Embedded Framework (about
          350&nbsp;MB). The <a href={docs.building}>README</a> walks you through it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href={docs.building} class="btn btn-secondary"><Icon name="terminal" size={18} />Build instructions</a>
        <a href={repo.url} class="btn btn-secondary"><Icon name="code" size={18} />Source code</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="switch-title" class="mt-16">
      <h2 id="switch-title" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">Before you switch</h2>
      <div class="prose mt-3">
        <ul>
          <li>Expect breaking changes, including to the data Magnetite keeps on disk.</li>
          <li>On Intel Macs and Linux, sites that only serve H.264 video or AAC audio do not play yet.</li>
          <li>Not there yet: several main windows, a small window for links from other apps, notes.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="legal-title" class="mt-16">
      <h2 id="legal-title" class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">Licence and licensor</h2>
      <div class="prose mt-3">
        <p>
          Magnetite is free software under the <a href="/license/">European Union Public Licence v1.2</a>. Every package
          contains the licence and the third-party notices; the source code is on <a href={repo.url}>GitHub</a>. Who
          publishes it: see the <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
